  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe central idea is to employ a hybrid optimization framework combining gradient-based refinement with a structured, randomized initialization based on periodic patterns. Unlike previous methods that relied on static cluster configurations, this approach introduces a dynamic initialization mechanism that adapts to the problem's symmetry. By leveraging the periodic nature of the overlap integral, we can construct candidate solutions that inherently distribute mass to minimize worst-case overlap. This approach addresses the local optimum bottleneck by introducing systematic variations in initialization and using directional perturbations to explore critical regions of the search space.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nRepresentation: A step function $ h(x) $ over $ [0, 2] $ with $ n_{\\text{points}} $ samples, where $ 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 $ and $ \\sum h[i] = n_{\\text{points}} / 2 $. The objective is:\n\n$$\nC_5 = \\max_k \\left( \\int_0^2 h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) dx \\right) \\cdot dx\n$$\n\nConstraints:\n- $ \\sum h[i] = n_{\\text{points}} / 2 $ (equality constraint)\n- $ 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 $ (bound constraints)\n\nImplementation:\n- Use a Fourier-inspired construction to initialize $ h $\n- Apply directional perturbations along predefined symmetry axes\n- Combine with a gradient-based optimizer (L-BFGS-B)\n- Enforce constraints through Lagrange multipliers during optimization\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Input: $ n_{\\text{points}} $, initial_h_values (if available)\nb) Validate parent:\n   - If provided, reshape to $ (n_{\\text{points}},) $ and normalize to $ \\sum h = n_{\\text{points}} / 2 $\n   - If not provided, generate a base pattern\nc) Initialization:\n   - Generate a base function $ h_{\\text{base}} $ with:\n      i) $ m = 20 $ cluster centers spaced at intervals $ \\Delta x = 2/m $\n      ii) Each cluster has width $ w = 0.1 $, centered at positions $ x_j = j\\Delta x + 0.05 $\n      iii) Normalize to satisfy integral constraint\nd) Optimization loop:\n   i) For $ \\text{iter} = 1 $ to $ 500 $:\n      - Select random symmetry axis $ \\theta $ (0\u00b0, 45\u00b0, 90\u00b0, 135\u00b0)\n      - Perturb $ h $ along $ \\theta $ using rotation matrix:\n         $$\n         h_{\\text{perturbed}} = \\text{clip}(h \\cdot \\cos\\theta + (1-h) \\cdot \\sin\\theta, 0, 1)\n         $$\n      - Normalize $ h_{\\text{perturbed}} $ to satisfy integral constraint\n      - Evaluate objective $ C_5 $ using np.correlate with full mode\n      - Use L-BFGS-B to refine $ h_{\\text{perturbed}} $ with:\n         * Objective function: $ -C_5 $\n         * Bounds: $ (0.0, 1.0) $\n         * Constraints: $ \\sum h = n_{\\text{points}}/2 $\n         * Tolerance: $ 10^{-8} $\n         * Max iterations: 50\ne) Track best solution:\n   - Maintain a history of top 10 candidates\n   - Re-evaluate final candidate with exact evaluator\nf) Final fallback:\n   - If no valid candidate, return parent with penalty term $ 0.01 $\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\nDefault configuration:\n- $ n_{\\text{points}} = 500 $\n- Base clusters: $ m = 20 $\n- Perturbation angles: $ \\theta \\in \\{0^\\circ, 45^\\circ, 90^\\circ, 135^\\circ\\} $\n- Iterations: 500\n- Refinement steps: 50\n- Tolerance: $ 10^{-8} $\n\nVariations:\n- Cluster count: $ m \\in \\{10, 20, 30\\} $\n- Perturbation angles: additional $ \\theta \\in \\{22.5^\\circ, 67.5^\\circ, 112.5^\\circ\\} $\n- Optimization method: switch to SLSQP if L-BFGS-B stalls\n- Perturbation frequency: 0.5 probability per iteration\n- Adaptive perturbation: increase angle range if C\u2085 stagnates\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\nTime allocation:\n- 100s: Initialization and base candidate creation\n- 300s: Optimization loop (500 iterations)\n- 100s: Final refinement and re-evaluation\n- 100s: Fallback preparation\n\nTermination checks:\n- After 500 iterations\n- If C\u2085 improvement < 1e-5 for 30 iterations\n- If remaining time < 30s\n\nRobustness measures:\n- Clip values to [0,1] after all operations\n- Use scipy.optimize.minimize with method='L-BFGS-B'\n- Add penalty term $ \\lambda (\\sum h - n/2)^2 $ to objective\n- Re-scale solutions after clipping using:\n   $$\n   h_{\\text{scaled}} = \\frac{h}{\\sum h} \\cdot \\frac{n}{2}\n   $$\n\n6. Validation and return contract\nFeasibility checks:\n- $ \\text{np.allclose}(np.sum(h), n_pts/2, atol=1e-6) $\n- $ np.all((h >= 0) & (h <= 1)) $\n\nObjective consistency:\n- Re-evaluate final candidate using exact evaluator:\n   $$\n   \\text{score} = \\max(\\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, mode=\"full\") * dx)\n   $$\n\nSanity checks:\n- $ \\text{score} \\leq 0.38085 $\n- $ \\text{np.sum}(h) == n_pts / 2 $\n- $ \\text{np.min}(h) \\geq 0 $, $ \\text{np.max}(h) \\leq 1 $\n\nFallback protocol:\n- If no valid solution found, return parent with penalty:\n   $$\n   h_{\\text{fallback}} = \\text{clip}(h + 0.01 \\cdot \\text{random\\_noise}, 0, 1)\n   $$\n   $$\n   \\text{score}_{\\text{fallback}} = \\max(\\text{np.correlate}(h_{\\text{fallback}}, 1-h_{\\text{fallback}}, mode=\"full\") * dx) + 0.01\n   $$",
